  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "One CHO is oxidised to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and one CHO is reduced to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> .<br /><br />Thus, it is not a disproportionation reaction. It is intramolecular redox reaction. Thus, option A and B are true and <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/eeeD.JPG\" style=\"width: 60px; height: 87px;\" /> is reducing as well as oxidising agent.<br /><br />Thus, option D is also true and option C is incorrect.",
